{"repositoryId":629981358,"availability":"available","full":"es-joy/jsoe","name":"jsoe","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2023-04-19T12:24:27Z","updated":"2026-10-13T02:17:00Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://es-joy.github.io/jsoe/demo/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:42.853Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:42.853Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:42.853Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T06:39:42.853Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["[](badges/tests-badge.svg) [](badges/coverage-badge.svg)","A query node is not fully self-describing in isolation - it is meant to be read back alongside the schema it was built from, not as a standalone format. Most leaf kinds don't repeat type information the schema already carries at that path; the deliberate exception is range's own valueType field, needed because five different schema types (number, NumberObject, bigint, date, buffersource) share one leaf shape, and two of them (bigint, date) even serialize their bounds as the same JS type (a plain string) - without valueType, a host couldn't otherwise tell a bigint range from a date range from…","This isn't applied evenly, though. range's valueType is an explicit, self-contained tag - a host only has to check one field. Several composite widgets instead rely on position, not any tag at all: regexpSearchType.js combines its source leaf (regex/literalSet/notContains) with an optional flags leaf at the same path via one $and (combineAnd([sourceLeaf, flagsLeaf])), so a bare multiSelect leaf found there means \"flags\" only because a host already knows regexp's own fixed two-leaf convention - nothing on the leaf itself says so, unlike range. The same bare multiSelect shape is also how…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/es-joy/jsoe/blob/